# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alteryx source workflows — NEVER COMMIT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .yxmd/.yxmc/.yxwz files embed credentials that Alteryx "encrypts" with a
# reversible, machine-local scheme. In this estate they carry:
#   * the Sybase ASE ODBC password (user U_ITMONITOR, DSN=SYBASE)
#   * a SendGrid API key (smtp.sendgrid.net, username "apikey")
#   * internal topology (\\swap629 shares, bacen.dbo.* table names)
# Publishing one exposes read access to BMG core-banking data and the ability
# to send mail as @bancobmg.com.br. Keep them out of version control.
*.yxmd
*.yxmc
*.yxwz

# Alteryx run artefacts / temp
*.yxdb
*.rptx
*.bak

# Outputs of the indicator — audit data, not code
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials & local config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.databrickscfg
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml

# Databricks bundle local state (contains workspace paths / deploy identity)
.databricks/
bundle.tf.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
